.TH mbphotomosaic 1 "7 September 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbphotomosaic\fP \- Generate a georeferenced photomosaic image from a set of navigated downlooking seafloor photographs.

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
mbphotomosaic [\fB\-\-verbose\fP \fB\-\-help\fP \fB\-\-threads=\fP\fInthreads\fP
\fB\-\-input=\fP\fIimagelist\fP \fB\-\-output=\fP\fIfile\fP
\fB\-\-output\-tiff\fP \fB\-\-output\-png\fP
\fB\-\-image\-dimensions=\fP\fIwidth\fP/\fIheight\fP
\fB\-\-image\-spacing=\fP\fIdx\fP/\fIdy\fP[/\fIunits\fP]
\fB\-\-sensor\-size=\fP\fIwidth\fP/\fIheight\fP[/\fIcellsize\fP]
\fB\-\-fov\-fudgefactor=\fP\fIfactor\fP \fB\-\-projection=\fP\fIprojection_pars\fP
\fB\-\-altitude=\fP\fItarget\fP/\fIrange\fP | \fB\-\-standoff=\fP\fItarget\fP/\fIrange\fP
\fB\-\-priority\-weight=\fP\fIweight\fP
\fB\-\-priority\-heading=\fP\fItarget\fP/\fIfactor\fP/\fImode\fP
\fB\-\-trim=\fP\fItrim_pixels\fP \fB\-\-section=\fP\fIsection_pixels\fP
\fB\-\-section\-length\-max=\fP\fIvalue\fP \fB\-\-rangemax=\fP\fIrange_max\fP
\fB\-\-bounds=\fP\fIlonmin\fP/\fIlonmax\fP/\fIlatmin\fP/\fIlatmax\fP \fB\-\-bounds\-buffer=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-correction\-brightness\fP \fB\-\-correction\-camera\-settings\fP
\fB\-\-correction\-range=\fP\fItarget\fP/\fIcoeff\fP
\fB\-\-correction\-standoff=\fP\fItarget\fP/\fIcoeff\fP
\fB\-\-correction\-file=\fP\fIimagecorrection.yaml\fP
\fB\-\-reference\-gain=\fP\fIgain\fP \fB\-\-reference\-exposure=\fP\fIexposure\fP
\fB\-\-reference\-intensity=\fP\fIintensity\fP
\fB\-\-reference\-crcb=\fP\fIintensity\fP/\fIintensity\fP
\fB\-\-dark\-image\-ignore=\fP\fIthreshold\fP
\fB\-\-dark\-image\-multiply=\fP\fIthreshold\fP/\fIfactor\fP
\fB\-\-platform\-file=\fP\fIplatform.plf\fP \fB\-\-camera\-sensor=\fP\fIid\fP
\fB\-\-nav\-sensor=\fP\fIid\fP \fB\-\-sensordepth\-sensor=\fP\fIid\fP
\fB\-\-heading\-sensor=\fP\fIid\fP \fB\-\-altitude\-sensor=\fP\fIid\fP
\fB\-\-attitude\-sensor=\fP\fIid\fP
\fB\-\-use\-left\-camera\fP | \fB\-\-use\-right\-camera\fP | \fB\-\-use\-both\-cameras\fP
\fB\-\-calibration\-file=\fP\fIstereocalibration.yaml\fP
\fB\-\-navigation\-file=\fP\fIfile\fP \fB\-\-tide\-file=\fP\fIfile\fP
\fB\-\-image\-quality\-file=\fP\fIfile\fP \fB\-\-image\-quality\-threshold=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-image\-quality\-filter\-length=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-topography\-grid=\fP\fIfile\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBMbphotomosaic\fP generates a single georeferenced mosaic image from a set of
navigated downlooking photographs, typically taken from a camera or stereo
camera rig towed or flown close to the seafloor. The program reads single or
stereo pair images and their associated navigation, attitude, and camera
settings from an MB-System imagelist file, projects each image's pixels onto
either an assumed flat seafloor at a nominal standoff or an actual bathymetric
topography grid, and writes the projected pixels into a regular output raster
covering a specified geographic (or projected) area.
.P
Each output pixel of the mosaic is written from whichever contributing input
pixel is judged to have the highest priority. By default priority is based
purely on how close a pixel lies to the center of its source image
(pixels near the middle of a photograph are usually less distorted and less
vignetted than pixels near the edges); if \fB\-\-altitude\fP or \fB\-\-standoff\fP is
given, priority also favors pixels whose projected standoff distance is close
to a specified target value. Priority can additionally be biased by vehicle
heading using \fB\-\-priority\-heading\fP, for example to favor images taken while
running a particular compass heading. Pixels are also weeded out if their
line of sight is too vertical, if the projected slant range exceeds
\fB\-\-rangemax\fP, or if they fall in the black borders introduced by camera lens
undistortion (unless a fixed \fB\-\-trim\fP margin is set instead).
.P
Optional corrections can be applied to pixel intensity before it is written
into the mosaic: a fixed correction for recorded camera gain and exposure
settings, a simple brightness normalization, a range- or standoff-dependent
correction using a supplied target/coefficient pair, or the pixel-position-
and-standoff-dependent 3D correction table produced by
\fBmbgetphotocorrection\fP. Reference intensity and color values, as well as
handling of unusually dark images (either ignored outright or boosted by a
multiplicative factor), can also be specified. Camera images can be
undistorted and, for stereo pairs, restricted to the left camera, the right
camera, or both, using a supplied stereo camera calibration file.
.P
The output raster's dimensions, pixel spacing, geographic bounds, and map
projection can all be controlled explicitly; if left unspecified, suitable
defaults are derived from the imagelist's navigation, the target standoff, and
the camera field of view. The output image is written as a GeoTiff or PNG file
according to the output filename's suffix, or as forced by
\fB\-\-output\-tiff\fP/\fB\-\-output\-png\fP. \fBMbphotomosaic\fP can process images
using multiple threads (see \fB\-\-threads\fP), and can incorporate an external
tide correction, a per-image quality filter, and an MB-System platform offset
model in the same manner as \fBmbgetphotocorrection\fP.

